    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Investigators report that Dong Fang Yu Liang buried large numbers of Charred Thunder Potato Gu under the defense line. The chain of blasts stops Hei tribe pursuit while remnant troops escape. It is still only rank two with limited power when used alone, and the mass count is credited for the effect. Mixed among them are many rank three muffled thunder potato Gu and a few rank four thunderclap potato Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          515
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "northern-plains-defense-line",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_dong_fang_yu_liang",
          "fac_hei_tribe",
          "gu_muffled_thunder_potato_gu",
          "gu_thunderclap_potato_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Cited chapters describe the explosive grass Gu without naming a cultivation path for this Gu.",
        "chapters": [],
        "certainty": "inferred",
        "confidence": "C",
        "verification": "no_citation",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "path",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ]
  },
  "appearance": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "The unplanted fruit is finger-thick and dark green. When refined and fed primeval essence, it gives off a faint green light, slowly hovers, then drills into the ground. Buried in soil, that tiny grass Gu grows into a fist-sized potato.",
        "chapters": [
          213
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "appearance",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "The fruits are Charred Thunder Potato Gu, a rank two Gu. After burial and growth, a matured one is fist sized and can explode from even a slight vibration. When refined and fed primeval essence, one fruit gives off a faint green light, hovers, then drills into the ground.",
        "chapters": [
          213
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "form-and-rank",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Those fruits come from Charred Thunder Potato Mother Gu, a rank three Gu that looks like a potato with an uneven surface and tiny holes. Primeval essence makes green sprouts grow from the holes, blossom, and bear dark green finger-thick fruit.",
        "chapters": [
          213
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "form-and-rank",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_charred_thunder_potato_mother_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Charred Thunder Potato Mother Gu also produces Charred Thunder Potato Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          256
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "form-and-rank",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ],
    "visual_confidence": "text_described"
  },
  "abilities": {
    "activation_raw": null,
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Once buried, the Gu grows with soil fertility. When any living being steps near it, vibration makes it self-detonate.",
        "chapters": [
          213
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Bai Mo Xing later calls it an expendable type that absorbs energy from the ground to grow and explodes after vibration impact, with strong attacking power among rank two Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          217
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_bai_mo_xing"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "It is an offensive Gu that cannot be moved once planted, which lowers its practical value. Layered burial can stack blasts strong enough that even thousand beast kings might not get off easy.",
        "chapters": [
          213
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_attack_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Planting itself spends aperture primeval essence while soil fertility gathers into the Gu and it swells from a tiny grass Gu to fist size.",
        "chapters": [
          213
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "That growth cost is separate from any later feed schedule the novel never states for unplanted fruits.",
        "chapters": [],
        "certainty": "inferred",
        "confidence": "C",
        "verification": "no_citation",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "It must be used in soil, and more fertile soil is better. On Bai Gu mountain, where there is no soil and the rocks are bone, it cannot be planted.",
        "chapters": [
          217
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "limits",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_bai_gu_mountain"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "It is unstable in use: it needs to be planted, fails if nobody steps on it, and a forgetful planter can injure themselves.",
        "chapters": [
          222
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "limits",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Chen Cui Hua buries many Charred Thunder Potatoes before her cave and later uses them against a twin-headed boar; Fang Yuan and Bai Ning Bing watch those traps go off.",
        "chapters": [
          210
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "early-use",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_chen_cui_hua",
          "char_bai_ning_bing"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "After killing her, Fang Yuan takes a charred thunder bean mother Gu among her aperture Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          211
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "early-use",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "He and Bai Ning Bing then produce and bury many Charred Thunder Potato Gu in layered pits to kill grass-skirt monkey kings.",
        "chapters": [
          213
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "early-use",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "He later buries at least five in a black bear’s retreat path during the Bai clan hunt.",
        "chapters": [
          217
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "early-use",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "fac_bai_clan_bai_gu_mountain"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Tie Dao Ku later reads an explosion site as almost a hundred Charred Thunder Potato Gu buried together, a trap that killed Tie clansmen during the chase after Fang Yuan and Bai Ning Bing.",
        "chapters": [
          220
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "early-use",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_tie_dao_ku"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
